# ---- Qwen / DashScope (OpenAI-compatible) ----
# Server-side only. NEVER expose these to the browser.
# Get a key from Alibaba Cloud Model Studio: https://console.aliyun.com/product/dashscope
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# OpenAI-compatible base URL. Defaults to the China endpoint if empty.
# China:      https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# International: https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
QWEN_BASE_URL=https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1

# Model name. Swap without changing business logic.
# Recommended V1 default: qwen3-coder-next
# If quality is unstable, try: qwen3-coder-plus
QWEN_MODEL=qwen3-coder-next

# If DASHSCOPE_API_KEY is empty, the app runs in DEMO MODE:
# /api/generate and /api/modify use a built-in offline template engine so the
# full create -> preview -> modify -> persist loop is testable without a key.
# Set the key above to use the real model.

# ---- Optional: Supabase (real server-side persistence) ----
# V1 ships with localStorage persistence enabled by default (works with zero setup).
# To upgrade to a real database, set these and implement lib/supabase.ts using
# the schema in supabase/schema.sql. See README for details.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
